neo is a brutal action RPG that demands  you to understand its systems in order  to overcome its challenges but with so  many mechanics at play it can be  overwhelming  that's why we've gathered 10 tips to  help you become a master samurai if you  enjoyed this video be sure to LIKE and  subscribe to our YouTube channel for  more features on how to not die in neo  to see more of the game in action check  out our dual swords gameplay video  [Music]  make sure to keep a close eye on your  key gauge during battle avoid recklessly  swinging your weapon at opponents as  it'll quickly drain your key and put you  in in a mobile state this is indicated  by a red gauge and while in this state  you're vulnerable to enemy attacks if  this occurs mash the Dodge button to  ensure you get out of the way of danger  as soon as possible unlike the souls  games you can see how much key an enemy  has when you lock onto them  when an opponent completely drains their  key they'll either lack the energy to  move or attack more erratically take  advantage of this opportunity as enemies  are more susceptible to being staggered  when you hurt them in this state when an  enemy is staggered you have a better  chance of landing a powerful grapple or  final below as well it's also possible  to inflict direct damage to an  opponent's key using special skills that  are acquired via the learned skills menu  each weapon type has a particular  technique that can inflict key damage  for example the sword has a kick skill  which allows you to chain a kick at the  end of a combo to drain an opponent's  key prioritize unlocking these skills as  they can be vital in overcoming tough  encounters  [Music]  one of the most important mechanics in  neo is the key pulse a combat maneuver  that allows you to restore some of the  key you've expended from attacking to  execute it press r1 when light gathers  around you after an attack the better  you timed the key pulse the more key  you'll gain back key pulse is also a  necessity in purifying yokai realms  which are enemy attacks that reduce your  key regeneration rate within a certain  area a perfect key pulse can instantly  remove yokai realm from the field to  execute a perfect key pulse time your  button press to when the light is just  about to fade around you you'll know  when you've executed it when a swirling  light forms as you raise your weapon the  benefits of key pulse may not seem like  much at first but using it effectively  can make all the difference in battle  it's important to take advantage of the  various weapon stances as each add  useful attack variations to the weapons  in your arsenal there are three stances  in total high mid and low high stance  offers large attack damage and defense  against enemies but at heavy expense to  your speed and key midstance offers  medium attack speed and damage with some  cost to your key and low stance allows  you to attack quickly I'll be it weekly  with little expense to your key  familiarize yourself with the feel of  each stance and how they impact your  weapons of choice some stances prove  more useful than others during certain  encounters utilizing a swords high  stance allows you to slash vertically  which is ideal against enemies that stay  low to the ground a careful and  calculated understanding of weapon  stances is key to surviving the most  difficult battles neo has an internal  achievement system called titles which  allows you to earn additional stat  bonuses there are two achievement lists  in total audio and in Gil each offers  different challenges that demand you  fulfill distinct conditions for instance  the swordsmen adept title requires you  to defeat 100 human enemies with the  sword the more you diversify the types  of attacks you use including non weapon  attacks like throwing bombs the more  likely you'll earn a new title upon  earning a title you will receive  reputation points  once you've accumulated enough you'll  gain a prestige point which you can use  to acquire a stat bonus in the prestige  summary screen  each piece of armour you find has its  own distinct special effects that grant  you a variety of bonuses such as damage  reduction  elmerita bonuses and increased -  endurance however in order to access  them you need to meet the armored  statistical parameters which are listed  at the bottom of its description in the  equipment screen for instance the foot  piece of the warlord armor requires your  stamina to be at seven in your strength  at six be mindful of parameters when you  equip armor is not meeting them makes a  piece of armor only half as useful as it  could be while it might not seem  apparent at first there's actually an  equipment weight mechanic in the game  each piece of armor has its own weight  value which when equipped contributes to  your overall equipment weight percentage  note how the font color changes from  green to yellow at the top of the  equipment screen when you exceed a  certain weight the higher the percentage  is the more key your attacks and dodges  will consume your movement speed is also  affected understand your play style to  manage your equipment weight accordingly  if you value mobility staying at a  lighter weight is ideal but if you  prefer slow powerful weaponry stick to a  heavier weight it's important that you  never let your equipment weight exceed  100% as your attacks and evasive  maneuvers will consume nearly half your  key per action  [Applause]  when you explore an area keep an eye out  for Kodama which are small green yokai  that wear soup cups as hats  if you encounter a Kodama approach it  and hold circle to send it back to a  shrine for every 5 you collect you  increase the max number of elixirs you  can hold at a time in addition the  number you collect affects the  percentages of the Kodama blessings you  receive at a shrine  [Music]  collecting Kodama also gives you access  to their blessings which are passive  buffs that you can purchase at a shrine  each blessing is associated with a  specific type of Kodama there are five  types in total with five of each defined  in a region the more you collect of a  specific type the higher the percentage  its respective blessing will be it's  important to note that whenever you  reach a new region the Kodama blessing  percentage is reset this is because each  region has its own set of 25 Kodama to  collect  [Music]  there are two special support abilities  in the game ninjutsu and own mule jutsu  ninjutsu focuses on the use of throwable  items and inflicting status ailments on  enemies while oh no jutsu emphasizes  imbuing your weapon with different  elemental properties to take advantage  of enemy weaknesses both are incredibly  useful and each offers you an array of  options to supplement your offensive  efforts ninjutsu and omiyo jutsu  abilities are unlocked by spending  points via the learned skills menu in  their respective tabs once you've  acquired a ninjutsu or onmyo jutsu skill  you can then assign one to an item  shortcut by accessing the Redi jutsu  menu if there are any beginners tips  that I missed shouted in the comments  below and for more neo coverage  including our full review be sure to  subscribe to our YouTube channel  [Music]  [Applause]  you
 

